;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">3. Experiment Model</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Operational levers in autonomous video production possess vastly different cost structures, execution latencies, and platform touchpoints. The engine models experiments across four concrete categories:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_2-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Creative Experiments</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Evaluate core viewer engagement drivers within the video narrative. Levers include hook structural frameworks (e.g., cold opens versus context-setting introductory questions), initial 30-second pacing (words per minute), narrative tension arcs, scene duration density, visual transition frequency (seconds per visual cut), and voice synthesis modulation (cadence, pitch range, emotional coloration).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Packaging Experiments</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Evaluate initial viewer discovery and click conversion. Levers include title syntax patterns, thumbnail focal layouts (e.g., single subject close-up versus multi-element curiosity tension), color palette contrast ratios, visual text overlay phrasing, and description structural schemas.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Production Experiments</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Evaluate asset composition, aesthetic quality, and rendering pipelines. Levers include asset class mix (programmatic 2D typography versus generative AI diffusion imagery), deterministic keyframed motion graphics versus AI camera motion, closed-caption typographic layouts, and audio mixing balances (speech-to-background music ducking ratios).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Operational Experiments</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Evaluate compute resource utilization, agent workflow configurations, and production pipeline throughput. Levers include deep-research web retrieval depth, multi-agent reflection pass counts, video render resolution and encoding profiles, and worker concurrency parameters.</span></li></ul><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">To ensure empirical validity, the engine stric