t;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Published Video Artifacts with Policy Metadata</span></p></td></tr><tr style="height:0pt"><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:117pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Layer 5: Canary Monitor &amp; Circuit Breaker</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:117pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">48-hour and 7-day metric evaluation, regression detection, automated policy rollback</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:117pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">spotify-confidence, bsts-causalimpact</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:117pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Automated Rollback Commands &amp; Audit Logs</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">End-to-End Operational Lifecycle</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The complete production lifecycle executes through eight sequential steps:</span></p><ol class="lst-kix_list_1a-0 start" start="1" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Evidence Ingestion</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Layer 1 ingests stratified 48-hour to 14-day post-publication metrics from YouTube Analytics, identifies outliers, verifies counterexamples, and emits a structured evidence packet.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Candidate Compilation</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Layer 2 compiles the evidence into a DecisionCandidate, evaluating proposed parameter deltas against negative knowledge stores, active risk budgets, and the Lexicographic Objective Hierarchy.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Experiment Design</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Layer 2 provisions an experiment in experiment_registry, determining sample size via CUPED variance reduction, setting mSPRT stopping boundaries, and selecting the study design (native split vs. matched pair).</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Policy Serialization</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Layer 2 emits a new Challenger policy document (vX.Y.Z-CHALLENGER), committing the operational intent to decision_ledger.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Autonomous Generation</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Hermes reads the Challenger policy, executes asset generation, enforces technical QA constraints, and publishes the video, embedding policy and experiment lineage IDs into the artifact record.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Interim Monitoring</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Layer 5 ingests early performance metrics at 48-hour intervals, computing mSPRT e-values and non-inferiority margins via spotify-confidence.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Circuit Breaker Check</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: If a canary upload trips retention or quality circuit breakers, Layer 5 aborts the trial and instantly re-pins the active Champion policy in the ledger.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Decision Resolution</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Upon crossing the efficacy boundary (\tilde{\Lambd[span_137](start_span)[span_137](end_span)a} \ge 1/\alpha), the Challenger is promoted to ACTIVE_CHAMPION, committed to the ledger, and established as the new baseline for Hermes. If inconclusive or futile, the experiment is archived in failed_hypotheses, preserving institutional memory.</span></li></ol><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12.8pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Operating an autonomous production engine on a dynamic recommendation platform requires treating channel stability as an engineering invariant rather than an optimization afterthought. By decoupling statistical evaluation from prompt orchestration and anchoring all production modifications in an append-only, version-controlled policy ledger, the system transforms noisy post-publication data into reliable, compounding institutional knowledge. Hermes pursues creative and operational breakthroughs within mathematically defined safety envelopes, ensuring that every upload advances channel authority without exposing the underlying infrastructure to catastrophic algorithmic drift or self-reinforcing failure loops.</span></p><h4 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:12pt;padding-bottom:12.8pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Works cited</span></h4><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">1. A/B test titles &amp; thumbnails - YouTube Help, https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/16391400?hl=en 2. YouTube Thumbnail &amp; Title A/B Testing - Feedzy, https://feedzy.io/youtube-ab-testing 3. How to A/B Test on YouTube: Tools and Strategies - TubeBuddy, https://www.tubebuddy.com/blog/how-to-a-b-test-on-youtube-youtube-a-b-testing-tools-and-strategies/ 4. spotify/confidence: Python library for AB test analysis - GitHub, https://github.com/spotify/confidence 5. confidence/HISTORY.rst at master - GitHub, https://github.com/spotify/confidence/blob/master/HISTORY.rst 6. YouTube Thumbnail A/B Testing Tools: Complete Comparison, https://www.tubeanalytics.net/blog/youtube-thumbnail-ab-testing-tools 7. YouTube Thumbnail Downloader (All Resolutions, Free) - Statly, https://statly.in/youtube-thumbnail-downloader 8. Stop Early Without P-Hacking Using mSPRT and Sequential Testing, https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/stop-early-without-p-hacking-using-msprt-and-sequential-testing-in-python/ 9. YouTube A/B Testing: Test &amp; Compare Thumbnails - vidIQ, https://vidiq.com/blog/post/youtube-launches-new-thumbnail-testing-tool/ 10. Feature request: expose "Test &amp; compare" (thumbnail/title A/B, https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/536234341 11. YouTube's API Quota Is 10,000 Units/Day. Here's How I Track 100K, https://dev.to/siyabuilt/youtubes-api-quota-is-10000-unitsday-heres-how-i-track-100k-videos-without-hitting-it-5d8h 12. Issue with Thumbnail updates via verified YouTube API, after using, https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/373328645 13. youtube-skills/references/thumbnail-principles.md at main - GitHub, https://github.com/sergebul